        "math_academy_id": "q-142113",
        "problem": "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $2x+4y\\ge 8?$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y & \\ge 8 \\\\ 4y & \\ge -2x+8 \\\\ y & \\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **solid line**.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/226415c7de8240eaa2a87a10e87d95c6dbf45df6263c4b36ea819cfec097a8a0.png)",
